[test-suite name=journal ring=2
  [doc [#
conformance fixtures for cx-stdlib/journal (spec/02-inprogress/xap/stdlib_journal.md
§3/§6/§10). Each program imports the bundled module via [?lib 'cx-stdlib/journal']
(resolver MUST be quoted). The LAST expression is the rendered result.

   journal is the append-only, hash-chained, tenant-partitioned event log +
   deterministic fold→state, built ON store (persistence) + hash (chain links)
   + crypto.ed25519 (snapshot signing). The four-channel model (code.md §9.1.2):
     - a committed entry is a present [entry] VALUE;
     - a failed-precondition append (stale-tail / closed / read-only / denied)
       is an [err] (failure channel);
     - an empty / out-of-range read is the ABSENCE channel — the empty
       node-set () — never null and never [err];
     - a verify / snapshot-verify of a corrupt chain is a present
       [verification valid=false …] / [snapshot-verification valid=false …]
       FINDING (a VALUE, not [err] — SAP §1).

   HERMETIC. Every case uses the mem:// backend (capability-free, deterministic)
   so fixtures need no host grant; the one file:// case is a CXER0271 denial
   (deny-lane). The default clock is a synthetic monotonic counter (ts =
   epoch:HH:MM:SS keyed off seq) so ts/hash are byte-stable across runs.

   Determinism: the entry hash is computed over the canonical CX bytes of
   seq+tenant+actor+authority+ts+prev-hash+event; genesis prev-hash is the
   fixed sentinel b3:GENESIS. The fold/replay/dry-run/snapshot/fold-from
   reducers MUST be pure (an impure $fn → CXER4611).

   Snapshot signing uses an ed25519 seed (32 bytes, hex) as opts.signing-key;
   the fixtures use the all-0x01 seed. mem:// may take an unsigned snapshot
   (opts.sign=false) usable for fold-from but NOT as a retention cover.

   Error band CXER4600–4649 (§8). Shared codes: CXER0271 (store cap denial).

   Id ranges:
     001-010  open/append/read/slice/since/head round-trip + chain link + absence
     011-018  fold / fold-slice / fold-value / replay / dry-run / determinism
     019-026  verify / verify-slice (finding-is-a-value) + tamper finding
     027-035  snapshot / snapshot-verify / fold-from (signed + unsigned + equivalence)
     036-041  retain / compact (prune-behind-snapshot + copy-forward source-intact)
     042-058  negatives / no-surface (every CXER46xx + CXER0271 denial)
     059-071  per-stream (§2.1.1) genesis / independence / verify / fold /
              snapshot / retain+compact
     072-075  appointed-signer surface (S6.4, §3.7/§4.8): the unsigned
              signer= outer hint (stamped, resolved, forged) + the opt-in
              require-appointed check against an [authz-store] registry
     078      sig-algo fail-closed: an unknown signature suite is
              :unsupported-suite via the suite-registry gate, never a
              fall-through Ed25519 attempt (#702/L36)
     084      stripped-tag downgrade (#691 §10): sig-algo ABSENT while a
              signature rides the snapshot is :unsupported-suite — the
              unsigned tier is only for snapshots carrying NO signature
     085      per-algo digest vectors (#691 §10): the four 1.0 registry
              algos over the SAME M5 commerce order document — tagged
              self-describing entry hashes (64/96/128/64 hex), payload=
              stays the Tier-1 sha2-256 document address in all four
     086-088  keep-after-time retention (#712 item 2): TS→seq boundary via
              §4.3 ts monotonicity (was a spec'd no-op) — boundary match,
              before-first keep-all (B=0), malformed-ts CXER4610
     089-098  stream-7 consistency vocabulary (#679, L122-L126): the
              declare-and-verify handle floor (accept + advert-refusal +
              the two teaching refusals + closed-set/type-strict), the
              always-on at-seq pin guard below a pruned floor (CXER4991,
              replay + snapshot), the declared-:gapless vs silent-clamp
              discriminator pair, and the head-fresh contract (F1 — the
              stale/fresh file:// pair is journal_head_fresh_test.v)
     099-103  stream-7 W6: the sect-3.7 tenant SET snapshot (the
              :at-head-set cut substrate — pre-W6 a tenant snapshot over
              named streams silently signed the empty default chain), set
              verify naming the divergent stream, the M5 cut, the L125
              pin resolve-through arc, and the fold-from-on-set teaching
              refusal
     079-080  frozen preimage pins (#724, audit C1): 079 recomputes entry
              hashes (default + named stream) from the §4.2 entry-canonical
              form via $cx:hash (Tier-1 document identity) — clean-room =
              shipped, byte-exact; 080 verifies a shipped snapshot signature
              against the §4.8 snapshot-canonical form reconstructed via
              $format:canonical (VALUE-emission bytes, state unwrapped, no
              trailing newline — the OTHER basis)
   #]]

  [# ── 001-010: open / append / read / slice / since / head ───────────── #]

  [case id=journal-001-append-genesis level=core
   [tags journal append genesis chain entry]
   [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/journal']
[?let [= $j [$journal:open "mem://acme" "acme"]]
  [$journal:append $j [do :refund] {actor: "ops" authority: "d-77"}]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
[entry seq=1 tenant=acme actor=ops authority=d-77 ts='1970-01-01T00:00:01Z' prev-hash='genesis:' payload='sha2-256:1c28ab1fd422c356d61afc4be98fe2ff836d21b306487a4d67a62b40fc762ec5' hash='sha2-256:902dfe8cf83616e030e70ec30429c632601d4bd29308b757049706a3afb218a4' [event [do :refund]]]
#]]
  ]

